@* Page header (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/navigation.css</code></li>
    <li>CMS admin layout <code>src/DotNetForge.Web/Areas/Admin/Views/Shared/_AdminLayout.cshtml</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>The top of a screen: the title, one sentence of description and the screen's actions. In the CMS admin you don't write
    it - the layout renders it from <code>ViewData["Title"]</code>, <code>ViewData["Description"]</code> and an
    <code>Actions</code> section. Write the classes yourself in your own layouts and extensions. On a real screen the title is
    the page's <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>; the examples here use <code>&lt;h2&gt;</code> because this page has its own.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <header class="dnf-page-header">
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Pages <span class="dnf-badge">12</span></h2>
            <div class="dnf-page-header__actions">
                <dnf-button icon="download">Import</dnf-button>
                <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="plus">New page</dnf-button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="dnf-page-header__description">The site's page tree: URLs, menus and SEO.</p>
    </header>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="title-only" title="Title only" description="A row with just the title; the description and the actions are optional." layout="block">
    <header class="dnf-page-header">
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Audit logs</h2>
        </div>
    </header>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="description-beside" title="Description under the title, actions beside both" description="The CMS admin layout's form: title and description stacked in the row, the actions at the end of the same row." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-page-header">
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <div class="dnf-stack dnf-stack--sm">
                <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Webhooks</h2>
                <p class="dnf-page-header__description">Notify other systems when entries or media change.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="dnf-page-header__actions">
                <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="plus">New webhook</dnf-button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="with-breadcrumbs" title="With breadcrumbs" description="Breadcrumbs come before the title; a status badge can sit in the title." layout="block">
    <header class="dnf-page-header">
        <nav class="dnf-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
            <ol class="dnf-breadcrumbs__list">
                <li class="dnf-breadcrumbs__item"><a href="/admin/content">Content</a></li>
                <li class="dnf-breadcrumbs__item"><a href="/admin/content">Articles</a></li>
                <li class="dnf-breadcrumbs__item"><span aria-current="page">Spring release notes</span></li>
            </ol>
        </nav>
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Spring release notes <dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Published</dnf-badge></h2>
            <div class="dnf-page-header__actions">
                <dnf-button icon-end="external-link">View</dnf-button>
                <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="save">Save</dnf-button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="wrapping" title="Wrapping" description="When the row is too narrow the actions wrap below the title; the description stops at 48rem." layout="block">
    <header class="dnf-page-header">
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Content types</h2>
            <div class="dnf-page-header__actions">
                <dnf-button icon="download">Export schema</dnf-button>
                <dnf-button icon="upload">Import schema</dnf-button>
                <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="plus">New content type</dnf-button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="dnf-page-header__description">Content types define the fields of entries: text, numbers, dates, media, relations and repeatable groups. Entries are edited in the Content Manager and listed on pages with content lists.</p>
    </header>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="A margin utility beats the component's space below; a border separates the header from the content." layout="block">
    <header class="dnf-page-header mb-3 border-b border-border pb-3">
        <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
            <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Settings</h2>
        </div>
    </header>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="Unlayered CSS restyles the parts in a scope - here a larger title." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-page-header">
        <header class="dnf-page-header">
            <div class="dnf-page-header__row">
                <h2 class="dnf-page-header__title">Reports</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="dnf-page-header__description">Traffic and content figures of the last 30 days.</p>
        </header>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-page-header .dnf-page-header__title {
    font-size: var(--dnf-text-3xl);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-header</code></td><td>block</td><td>a column, gap <code>--dnf-space-2</code>, <code>--dnf-space-6</code> below</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-header__row</code></td><td>element</td><td>title and actions, wrapping, space between</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-header__title</code></td><td>element</td><td>the heading as a row, with room for a badge or icon</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-header__description</code></td><td>element</td><td>muted, at most 48rem wide</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-header__actions</code></td><td>element</td><td>a wrapping row of buttons</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There is no tag helper: the classes are the API. In CMS admin screens the layout writes them; a screen sets:</p>
<ui-doc-code id="admin-view" lang="razor">
@@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Pages";
    ViewData["Description"] = "The site's page tree: URLs, menus and SEO.";
}
@@section Actions {
    <dnf-button variant="Primary" icon="plus" href="/admin/pages/create">New page</dnf-button>
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The title is the page's only <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li>Breadcrumbs, when shown, come before it.</li>
    <li>Use <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> for the block when it is the page's own header; the admin layout uses a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>
        inside <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do put the primary action last in <code>dnf-page-header__actions</code>.</li>
    <li>Do keep the description to one sentence about what the screen is for.</li>
    <li>Don't repeat the page header's actions inside the content.</li>
</ul>
